CyberArk Discovery SVC Account Remediator
This is a one-time live-run script for discovered service accounts.
Source
```text
Safe     : AP-WPA-P-C1-AMNG-DISCOVERY
Platform : WIN-DOMAIN-E-PR0NENR-DISC
```
Target
The script reads the first three letters after `SVC` and maps them to:
```text
AP-<APPCODE>-P-C1-AMNG
```
Example:
```text
SVCWBK_SQL_APP -> WBK -> AP-WBK-P-C1-AMNG
```
Newly created target accounts use:
```text
WIN-DOMAIN-E-PR0NENR-STATIC
```
Live run
There is no preview mode and no per-account prompt.
```powershell
.\Remediate-DiscoverySvcAccounts.ps1 `
  -Environment prod `
  -ConfirmRun YES
```
What happens per account
```text
1. Read account from discovery Safe.
2. Confirm username starts with SVC + 3-letter app code.
3. Build target Safe name.
4. Check target Safe exists.
5. Check if the service account already exists in target Safe.
6. If it exists, delete discovery copy.
7. If it does not exist, retrieve secret, create account in target Safe, then delete discovery copy.
```
Existing match mode
Default:
```powershell
-ExistingMatchMode UsernameAndAddress
```
Alternative:
```powershell
-ExistingMatchMode UsernameOnly
```
CPM behavior
Default is conservative for the STATIC platform:
```text
TargetAutomaticManagementEnabled = false
```
To create the target accounts with Automatic Password Management enabled:
```powershell
.\Remediate-DiscoverySvcAccounts.ps1 `
  -Environment prod `
  -ConfirmRun YES `
  -TargetAutomaticManagementEnabled $true
```
Reports
Reports are written to `reports\`:
```text
Remediate-DiscoverySvcAccounts_Report_*.csv
Remediate-DiscoverySvcAccounts_Created_*.csv
Remediate-DiscoverySvcAccounts_DeletedDiscovery_*.csv
Remediate-DiscoverySvcAccounts_Skipped_*.csv
```
Logs are written to `logs\`.

Missing Source Secret Handling
If the discovered source account has no retrievable secret, the script will still onboard the target account by default.
Default behavior:
```text
UseGeneratedPlaceholderSecretWhenSourceSecretMissing = true
```
When the source secret cannot be retrieved, the target account is created with a generated temporary placeholder secret. The full placeholder value is never logged.
The report will show:
```text
SecretSource = GeneratedPlaceholder
SecretNote   = Source secret was not retrievable. Generated temporary placeholder secret was used. Validate/update password before enabling CPM.
```
To force the run to fail instead of using a placeholder secret:
```powershell
.\Remediate-DiscoverySvcAccounts.ps1 `
  -Environment prod `
  -ConfirmRun YES `
  -UseGeneratedPlaceholderSecretWhenSourceSecretMissing $false
```
